atlas surface

architecture queue-simulator
  canonical_name Process simulator
  family surface
  domain Surface / Queued work, staffing and flow
  layer application
  semantic_question For a process of stations joined by routes, with arrivals by hour or an exact trace, how long does work wait at each station, how many give up or are turned away, how busy are staff, and what hourly staff meets a waiting goal?
  purpose A Work Samples workspace built from the claude-skills capacity-planner donor as an instrument rather than prose: a draggable process map, a day strip where arrivals and hourly staff are edited directly, queueing formulas worked out on every edit, a seeded event simulation in a worker with 95% intervals across runs, playback of a simulated day on the map, run-against-run comparison, and real arrivals replayed from NYC 311 open data
  maturity implemented
  consumes NYC Open Data 311 Service Requests (erm2-nwe9), read live from the visitor's browser and once retained with its query and response digest
  publishes ProcessModel JSON, per-station results CSV, visit log CSV, share link
  node_types Station, Route, ArrivalProfile, ArrivalTrace, ServiceDistribution, HourlyStaffing, SimulationRun, Comparison
  internal_calculus Erlang C by the stable Erlang B recursion; M/M/c waits exact, other variability by the Allen–Cunneen correction, named as an approximation on the page
  internal_calculus traffic equations solved by repeated substitution; a cycle that never reaches the exit is reported instead of simulated
  internal_calculus non-homogeneous arrivals by thinning; exponential patience with lazy removal; queue limits turn work away; staff changes take effect at each hour
  internal_calculus a station's staff-hours a day become people by hours each and time away; a twelve-month hiring sequence sizes each month's starters so that, once ramped linearly and after monthly leaving, capacity meets that later month's need, and months that cannot be covered in time are reported
  internal_calculus staffing per hour is the smallest staff whose formula service level meets the station's goal; the simulation then checks it
  invariant every run is repeatable from its seed; replications use derived seeds so a comparison against a kept run uses the same draws
  invariant a difference between two runs is called better or worse only when the 95% intervals do not overlap
  invariant arrivals labelled as the city's records are the retained or live records; handling times, staff and patience are labelled as assumptions until a visitor replaces them
  invariant a model with routes not summing to 100%, staff outside 0–500 or no entry is described and not run
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/process-sim.test.mjs checks Erlang C against published values (11 agents at 10 erlangs, 0.6821), simulated wait, utilisation and service level inside the interval of the exact M/M/c answer, seed repeatability, routing proportions with a rework loop, abandonment and blocking, hourly staffing meeting its target by formula and in simulation, refusal of broken models, lognormal moments, timestamp and duration import, and interval-based comparison
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/queues-research-browser.mjs run against a local build on 2026-10-19 at 1440 and 390 px: forty people today against the found staffing produced a hiring sequence; a run finished, formula staffing raised the answered share from 42% to 87% in simulation, no sideways scroll
  witness packs/aurekai-work-samples/site/nyc311-phone-20261006.json retains 2,225 phone-created NYC 311 requests for Tuesday 6 October 2026 with the query and response SHA-256
  forbidden_inference a simulated staffing plan -> a hiring decision, a rota anyone has agreed to, or a forecast of a future day
  forbidden_inference a 311 service request created by phone -> a call handled by a 311 agent; calls that created no request are absent from the data
  forbidden_inference formula agreement with simulation -> agreement with the real operation; handling times in the example are assumptions
  known_gap not yet published to aurekai-work-samples.pages.dev; the deploy is the operator's to run
  known_gap no native save or continuation; work is kept in browser storage, a share link and downloaded files
  known_gap priorities between work types and skill-based routing are not modelled
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/process-sim.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/process-sim-worker.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/process-sim-client.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/process-sim-material.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/process-sim.css
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/simulation.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/process-sim.test.mjs
  source_path packs/aurekai-work-samples/site/nyc311-phone-20261006.json
  source_lineage 2026-10-19 claude-skills business-operations/skills/capacity-planner at 19392f7a; ChatGPT sandbox build rejected by Nick as faking

interaction service-site-packages-queue-simulator
  source service-site
  destination queue-simulator
  relation packages_workspace
  preserves the retained arrivals byte for byte with their query and digest, and the engine the tests run under one versioned asset prefix
  drops nothing a visitor edits; the package carries no visitor state
  forbidden_inference a packaged workspace -> a published one; publication is a separate deploy
  invalidates_on process-sim sources, retained arrivals, simulation section markup
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/process-sim-material.mjs
